e. It binds explicit audit, source and control identity anchors, checks canonical archive/receipt and metadata closure, and emits a deterministic transport inventory with retained generations. Floating entries use `no-store`; only versioned/content-addressed dependencies become shared immutable aliases. Existing non-digest-named RPM metadata remains a floating entry and is retained inside each snapshot.\n\nThe output is explicitly `plan_only`. It does not authenticate caller-supplied anchors, verify signatures/provenance, execute package contents, access credentials or networks, upload, activate or delete anything. Stable publication, production manifests, preview defaults and workflows remain unchanged. CDN switching and native-client A/B acceptance remain separate work.\n\nValidation:\n- 31 planner tests and 84 related tests passed; repository contract check passed.\n- Independent review verified bounded input reads, path/closure rejection, deterministic retention and the plain-name RPM classification. Its input-size finding was fixed with failure-first regressions.\n- Real public beta.24 immutable audit `402342684`: complete 308,536,832-byte archive digest and historical public control/source anchors checked; planner output independently matched all 44 archive files. Plan: 17 floating entries, 14 immutable aliases, SHA-256 `3c1dd765103ede4839f4d213d58bb8674365091d190008bc39ee84a289aed114`.\n- This real-input check is structural/byte consistency evidence, not cryptographic or public-client publication acceptance. Initial rejected inputs and subsequent fixes are preserved in the v3 readiness evidence.\n- First-attempt CI passed for `09360d07d0bffa3258be252d7730902041026ba8`: [Pages validation](https://github.com/WuKongIM/packages/actions/runs/39554961478) passed repository contracts and all 373 Python tests; [native TEST ONLY drill](https://github.com/WuKongIM/packages/actions/runs/39554961461) passed the seven isolated source-metadata cases, package build, signed 